I expect the kernel `conformance.kernel.recovered-from-prose` to move from 'no' to 'yes' when the input is a strict JSON object and the transform `conformance.transform.prose-before` is applied. According to the registry, this kernel tracks whether the harness had to recover the object from prose or a fence (yes) or read it as strict JSON (no). By adding the sentence 'Here is the form:' before the JSON object, the reply is no longer a strict JSON document, which should trigger the harness's recovery logic.